*******************************************************************************
* UNIVERSAL z/TPF .TDR GENERATOR TEMPLATE
* Purpose: Verify host output responses for each command before proceeding.
* Replace every <PLACEHOLDER>; remove unused examples before execution.
* Review environment, command authority, and expected responses with an operator.
*******************************************************************************
*
* GLOBAL UNEXPECTED STRINGS (optional; each GU is an abort condition)
* GU:<GLOBAL_UNEXPECTED_MESSAGE_ID_OR_TEXT>
*
* CASE 1 - command with one or more required response strings
C:<TPF_COMMAND_AND_PARAMETERS>
T:120
E:<EXPECTED_MESSAGE_ID_OR_TEXT>
* Add another E: only when ALL listed expected strings must appear:
* E:<SECOND_REQUIRED_RESPONSE_STRING>
* LU:<UNEXPECTED_RESPONSE_FOR_THIS_COMMAND>
*
* CASE 2 - command with no response assertion (use intentionally)
C:<COMMAND_THAT_DOES_NOT_REQUIRE_RESPONSE_CHECK>
*
* CASE 3 - additional command block
C:<NEXT_COMMAND>
T:120
E:<EXPECTED_RESPONSE>
*
* Notes:
* - Blank lines and comment lines are ignored by the TDR parser.
* - Each key/value entry must occupy one physical line.
* - C: begins a command block; E: lines following it are associated with that command
*   until another command block begins.
* - Multiple E: entries mean all expected strings are required (AND).
* - Multiple GU: or LU: entries behave as alternative unexpected matches (OR).
* - IBM documentation describes T:/TC: timeout range as >60 and <3600 seconds;
*   confirm the exact rule for the installed z/TPF level and runner.
* - TC: behavior and some advanced keys are RAVEN/TDRV-specific; do not add unless
*   the execution environment supports them.
